        ("BTLEServer", "The Bluetooth Low Energy daemon inside Apple's bluetoothd stack. It runs the constant low-power advertising and scanning that lets nearby Apple devices notice each other, which is how AirDrop targets appear and how Handoff knows your iPhone is next to your Mac."),
